<title>NETHERLANDS: Nedlloyd to shed 250 jobs after P&amp;O merger.</title>
<headline>Nedlloyd to shed 250 jobs after P&amp;O merger.</headline>
<dateline>ROTTERDAM 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch shipping and road transport firm Nedlloyd NV has reached agreement in principle with unions on roughly 250 job losses in the Netherlands after its $1.5 billion container shipping merger with Britain's P&amp;O, Nedlloyd said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Redundant employees will be offered open-ended contracts with an outplacement agency at a guaranteed salary, the company said, in order to avoid compulsory redundancies as far as possible.</p>
<p>Unions at the company have agreed to recommend the plan to their members, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
